00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.130
episode

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.130
"Oscar, Now is the Time

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.130
to Leave the Nest"

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.690
I am Colonel Girodelle, Regiment
Commander of the Royal Guards!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.130
To the National Assembly representatives
who are occupying the assembly hall!

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.230
If you continue your occupation of the hall,

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.020
you will be deemed as traitors who
have defied His Majesty's order.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.980
The Royal Guards Regiment will
be forced to remove you!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.940
Prepare to charge!

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:44.650
Wait!

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.450
Stay where you are, Regiment Commander!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.330
Fellow members of the nobility!
Follow my lead!

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.460
Marquis La Fayette.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.870
We're nobles,

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.310
but we're also in favor of participating in the National Assembly alongside the Third Estate representatives!

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.060
We won't let you lay a finger on
the commoners' representatives!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.250
Please step aside, Marquis La Fayette!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.020
Depending on the situation,
we're permitted to open fire!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.440
Forward, march!

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:24.660
Stay back!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.390
Stay back, stay back, stay back!

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.130
Commander!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.090
Girodelle, do you have the courage
to take my sword?!

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:43.300
Royal Guardsmen, do you have the courage to
pierce through my heart with your bayonets?!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.650
Then, fire!

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.050
If you intend to point your guns at the unarmed
representatives of the Third Estate,

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.230
you'll have to step over my dead body first!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.100
Mademoiselle.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.310
Please sheathe your sword.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.870
How could we ever shoot you,
our former commander?

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.540
How could we ever...

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.050
reduce ourselves to being cowards, who would
point our guns at unarmed men in front of you?

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.020
We'll wait for the day they take up arms.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.360
This is for you...

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.220
Even if this should condemn me as a traitor...

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.060
Girodelle...

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.160
Everyone, fall back!

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.630
Count!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.050
Count Jarjayes!

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.620
Of all people, your son—no, daughter...

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.280
Brigadier Oscar has openly ignored
His Majesty's order!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.660
This is an unforgivable treasonous offense!

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:08.850
The proper punishment would be to strip the Jarjayes family of its title and send Oscar into exile!

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.810
Lord Jarjayes, it's impossible for
me to defend you this time.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.370
Answer, Count Jarjayes!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.310
What are you going to do
about this misconduct?!

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:20.140
Your Majesty, please swiftly
hand down your punishment!

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.280
Brigadier Oscar's defiance is the
defiance of the Jarjayes family!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.620
I believe taking away their lands is fit punishment!

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:32.520
I'd like to discuss this matter with the Queen first.
Thoughts, everyone?

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:37.790
With all due respect, Your Majesty, it won't be
necessary for you to hand down your punishment,

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.030
as I, Jarjayes, will do away with
the traitor with my very own hands!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:52.640
My Lady, the Master...

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.950
I'm coming in, Father.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.160
Say, André, what happened?

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.300
The Master looked livid when
he said, ''Go get Oscar!''

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.370
Nothing really.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.630
It's nothing you should be
worried about, Grandma.

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.050
Sit here, Oscar.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.220
Are you prepared, Oscar?

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.820
Prepared for what?

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:40.690
Remove your military insignia and medals
that were given to you by His Majesty!

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.120
Allow me to ask again.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.610
What should I be prepared for?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.060
So you insist on being defiant
even in front of your father?!

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.370
I'll listen to any final words you may have.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.280
You may be a traitor, but you're still my daughter.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:00.750
Twelve of my men are imprisoned in Abbaye Prison
and will soon be executed by firing squad.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.460
If slaying me will save those 12 men,

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.250
I'll gladly give my life up to you, Father.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.320
But I'm afraid that's not how things work.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.760
Therefore, I cannot die here now!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.190
Give it up, Oscar!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:21.760
It's a tradition of the Jarjayes family to
remain loyal to His Majesty no matter what!

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.190
Now that we have a traitor
in the family, it's over!

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:29.190
Fear not, once I send you to the Lord,
I'll follow right behind you!

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:32.700
Then, that's all the more reason...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.160
...I cannot let myself be slain!

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:40.110
Such a kind child... but it's over now!

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.750
Please don't!

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.480
Let go! Let go, André!

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:11.350
I won't let you go!

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.700
If you're going to kill Lady Oscar, I'll never let go!

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.820
Get out of my way!

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:32.600
If you insist on killing her, I'll shoot
you and elope with Oscar!

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.170
What?!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.550
Elope with Oscar?!

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:36.970
Yes...!

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.470
Is that how you truly feel?

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:43.430
Yes.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.080
You fool!

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.650
Do you really think you can overcome the class
difference of a noble and a commoner?!

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.620
Then, allow me to ask you this!

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:53.890
What is ''rank?''

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.520
What is a ''commoner?''

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:56.970
All men are created equal!

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.830
A noble cannot marry without
the permission of His Majesty!

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.290
I'm aware of this!

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:08.290
But do you truly need permission, even
from His Majesty, to just love someone?!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.460
André!

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.460
Why you...!

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.440
I won't forgive either of you.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.110
Then,

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.570
please kill me first.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:41.030
Even though it'll only be a moment, if I die after,
I'll be forced to witness my love's death.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.580
I cannot... bear such sorrow.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:45.620
André...

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.150
All right, I'll grant your wish then!

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.930
Open the gate!

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:20.730
Count Jarjayes, please open the gate!

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:22.300
I have an urgent message!

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.370
It's an urgent message from Versailles!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.860
Please open the gate!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.540
By Her Majesty's grace,

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:37.510
''Brigadier Oscar François de Jarjayes and
the Jarjayes family will see no punishment!''

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:43.470
''Furthermore, your continued loyalty to the royal
family is expected,'' are Her Majesty's words!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.690
Lady Antoinette has...

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.950
Did you hear Her Majesty's merciful words?!

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:07.950
You've been spared... You fool...

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.110
You fool...

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.600
Prison of the Abbaye

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:27.740
So what's going to happen to us?

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.210
You idiot. What do you think?

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:32.110
We're going to be executed by firing squad
for treason, just like General Bouillé said.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:32.980
Right, Alain?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.150
Probably.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:39.610
But since we're officially enlisted in the military,
we should be able to have some sort of trial.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:44.990
Execution or not, I plan on giving
them a piece of my mind regardless.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.830
Yeah, you're right. All right!
I'm going to tell them off, too!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.250
Like raise our pay and giving us more time off!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:51.700
You idiot.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.580
What's the point of getting a break,
if we're going to be executed?

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.160
Oh, right.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:04.510
Listen closely.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.180
Your sentences have been handed down.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:09.450
Five days from now, at 8 o'clock in
the morning on the first of July,

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.440
you will all be executed by firing
squad at Louis XV Square.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.440
What?!

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:16.630
Wait a minute, Guard!

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.880
What about our military trial?!

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.990
We haven't been tried yet!

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:24.820
The military trial already took place.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.050
That can't be! We weren't called into court!

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.550
Maybe the bigwigs skipped that part?

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.850
It happens a lot.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.900
Damn it!

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.960
They convicted us in absentia!

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:45.260
Give it up, everyone! Let's all resign to our fate!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.590
André told me where I could find you.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:09.390
I need you to do me a favor, Bernard.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:12.630
All right, if it's within my power. However...

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:16.660
Count me out if it has anything to do with benefiting
the royal family or the nobility's greedy interests.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.600
It's for the sake of my 12 subordinates.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.130
They're all commoners.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.310
All right, go on.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:25.510
I owe you a debt.

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:28.470
What?

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.880
Surround Abbaye Prison?

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:34.120
Yes, if anyone, you should
be able to rally the people.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:37.420
A thousand... No, better yet,
I want you to rally at least 3000 people.

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:40.060
It's not impossible, but...

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.400
Will that really save your men though?

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.760
I'm the Commander of the French Guards, who is
responsible for keeping the peace in Paris.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:51.370
If I judge that Paris' security is in danger, I can
request the release of the 12 men to the King.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.340
I see.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:53.700
That's a good idea.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.830
We could really use someone as
clever as you on the commoners' side.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.040
Will you do it?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.810
There's one problem.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:03.500
What if it turns into a riot?

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:08.620
I promise that none of your comrades
or the people will get hurt or die.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.690
If I break my promise,
I'll leave the French Guards,

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:13.980
and run errands or do whatever
your group needs me to do.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:16.290
All right.

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:17.390
I'll give it a try.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:20.530
Watch and see how many people
will gather from my speech.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.500
I'm counting on you.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.630
Oscar, give André my regards.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:30.140
After this is all settled and done,
I'd like to see Rosalie.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:31.210
Please do.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.740
I'm sure Rosalie would be thrilled.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:33.530
See you then.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:45.840
I believe it's worth trying, but what are your
thoughts on it, Monsieur Robespierre?

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:50.800
''Save the 12 soldiers who have been convicted
in absentia and are about to be silenced.''

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:51.960
We should do it.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.450
If we succeed, we'll be able to draw in the
hearts of all the other soldiers to our cause.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:59.440
A day will come when we'll
have to fight the military.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.960
And when we do, if the
soldiers' hearts are on our side...

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.540
Why wait for that day to come?

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:08.100
Why don't we simply lead the gathered crowd
straight to the Palace of Versailles?

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.250
That's enough, Saint-Just!

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.320
Why do you always try to
take such extreme measures?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.050
Extreme?

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.020
Me?

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:21.230
Establishing the National Assembly,
saving the 12 soldiers...

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:22.930
...and the oath at Jeu de Paume!

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:26.420
Attaining great power requires
proper preparation and patience.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:31.570
You seem to be nothing more than
a bloodthirsty terrorist in my eyes.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:32.940
Come on, Monsieur.

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:35.940
I merely proposed a plan.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.890
If it doesn't suit you that'll be the end of it.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.680
Do it, Bernard!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:42.940
I pray that it'll be successful!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.280
We will now go on special patrol in Paris!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:56.240
We've been informed there will be
a rally at Palais-Royal Square today!

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.710
Our mission is to guard the rally from a distance!

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.970
Also, I have one rule I'd like you to follow!

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.900
Do not open fire on the people, no matter what!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:10.100
Do not open fire, even if they provoke us!

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:13.980
All mount!

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.090
Fall out!

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.980
I'm Bernard Châtelet!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.960
Everyone gathered here at Palais-Royal Square!
There's something I must tell you all!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:29.960
Fellow citizens!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:34.260
As you are all aware, our sons, yes,

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:36.910
even our fellow commoners' sons
are in the detestable military!

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:43.870
In fact, 12 of our sons are about to be executed
by firing squad without a proper trial!

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.840
Hey, this rally is to save Alain and the others!

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:48.340
Yeah!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.180
Fellow citizens!

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:53.450
People of Paris, who are willing
to bridge the new era!

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.590
Even though they're enlisted in
the military of the old regime,

00:17:56.590 --> 00:18:00.010
they are paid almost nothing and are
merely regarded as human shields!

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.730
I'd like you to know, they are our
comrades who deserve our compassion!

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:03.450
That's her.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.490
That's the Security Commander.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.860
Let's kill her.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:11.860
If we kill her, they'll ban the people
from holding public gathering.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.200
When that happens, the people
will become enraged and riot.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:19.310
Then, all we have to do is direct
the rioters towards Versailles.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.000
Fellow comrades!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:27.330
Let us all march to Abbaye Prison and
demand the release of those 12 men!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:30.420
Yeah! Bernard Châtelet is right!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.890
Let's all head to Abbaye Prison!

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:33.990
Wait! Think about it though!

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.490
If we head to Abbaye, the military isn't
going to just stand back and watch!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.660
Yeah, I don't want to get hurt!

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.650
No way, the military won't do anything.
Look at how many of us are here.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:55.990
Everyone, let's all march to the Abbaye!

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.950
Yeah! To the Abbaye!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.780
Save our 12 sons!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.200
Oscar!

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.330
Oscar, where are you?!

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:41.950
You're the leader of the terrorist group
that attacked Duke Ardelos, aren't you?!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.360
Stop!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.660
Release them!

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.720
Release them!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.870
Those 12 soldiers are the fellow
sons of us, commoners!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.120
Release them immediately!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.630
Release them!

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:39.350
Oscar!

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:40.480
Oscar!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:44.970
Oscar...!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.640
André, what's happening? How goes it?

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.050
It's a huge success!

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:51.600
Over 5000 people have surrounded the Abbaye!

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.880
All right, it worked!

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:01.430
An emergency! An emergency!

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:02.200
An emergency! An emergency!

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:06.070
We've just received an urgent message from
\hthe Company Commander of the French Guards!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:10.540
''Over 30,000 people have surrounded the Abbaye
and their numbers are continuing to grow!''

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:12.510
''The security is now beyond our control!''

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:14.580
''It is only a matter of time until
a riot breaks out,'' is the message!

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:16.510
You mustn't!

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:20.050
If you release those 12 men, the commoners
will become even more arrogant!

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:27.020
My Queen...

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:31.120
Your Majesty, what is there to be hesitant about?

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.390
Well, um...

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.620
Why are you all hesitating, as well?!

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:37.460
Release those 12 men at once!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:42.360
Are you willing to turn our beautiful Paris into
a sea of fire over the lives of just 12 men?!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:02.290
Alain, this is not Bernard's power
and certainly not mine, either.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:03.550
This is the power of the people!

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:09.160
Commander, it seems you're starting
to learn how this world really works.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:20.170
<i>On June 30, 1789, the people of Paris
took back their 12 soldiers.</i>

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:23.780
<i>This victory of the people, by the people...</i>

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:26.660
<i>...was nothing more than a small surging wave,</i>

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:29.920
<i>in comparison to the great wave that is soon to come.</i>

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:33.330
To be continued

